  "title": "Chinampas of Xochimilco",
  "summary": "The chinampas of Xochimilco are artificial garden plots built from lake sediment, branches and vegetation, separated by canals and edged with ahuejote willows. Developed around the lake shores in the pre-Hispanic Valley of Mexico and expanded with Tenochtitlan from 1325, they remain farmed in southern Mexico City.",
